From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marcho78 <marcho78@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] thermal/drivers/tegra/soctherm: Throttle at the hot trip's
 temperature again

tegra_soctherm_set_hwtrips() programs the hardware throttle with
"temperature", which by then holds the shutdown (thermtrip or critical)
temperature. Before commit 5136f99b9a4a, get_hot_temp() overwrote it with
the hot trip's temperature; get_hot_trip() returns the trip instead, and
its temperature is no longer used. Since then the hardware throttle
engages only at the shutdown temperature, so a Tegra210 board never
throttles before it powers off: "throttrip: will throttle when cpu
reaches 102500 mC" on the SHIELD TV 2017, whose cpu-thermal hot trip is
at 98500 mC (tegra210.dtsi).

Program the throttle at the hot trip's temperature.

Fixes: 5136f99b9a4a ("thermal: tegra: Use thermal_zone_for_each_trip() for walking trip points")
---
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/tegra/soctherm.c b/drivers/thermal/tegra/soctherm.c
index d8e988a0d..13a740a18 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/tegra/soctherm.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/tegra/soctherm.c
@@ -777,7 +777,7 @@ static int tegra_soctherm_set_hwtrips(struct device *dev,
 		else
 			continue;
 
-		ret = throttrip_program(dev, sg, stc, temperature);
+		ret = throttrip_program(dev, sg, stc, hot_trip->temperature);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "throttrip: %s: error during enable\n",
 				sg->name);
@@ -786,7 +786,7 @@ static int tegra_soctherm_set_hwtrips(struct device *dev,
 
 		dev_info(dev,
 			 "throttrip: will throttle when %s reaches %d mC\n",
-			 sg->name, temperature);
+			 sg->name, hot_trip->temperature);
 		break;
 	}
 
